<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Sequences-Question 1</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>List the first \(5\) terms of the following sequence.</p>
<p>\(\quad \quad \displaystyle \left\{ {@seq@} \right\}_{n=0}^{ \infty} \)</p>
<p><b>Hint:Give your answer in fraction form</b></p>
<p>\(1^{st} \text{term}=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p>\(2^{nd} \text{term}=\)[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>\(3^{rd} \text{term}=\)[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]][[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p>\(4^{th} \text{term}=\)[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]][[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p>\(5^{th} \text{term}=\)[[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]][[feedback:prt5]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution</b></p>
<p>Starting at \(n=0\) , plug in the first five values of \(n\) into the formula for the sequence terms.
</p>
<p>Doing that gives,</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \quad \quad n=0: \quad \frac{{@aa@}(0)}{(0)^2-{@bb@}}=0\)</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \quad \quad n=1: \quad \frac{{@aa@}(1)}{(1)^2-{@bb@}}=\frac{{@aa@}}{{@(1)^2-bb@}} ={@ta2@}\)</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \quad \quad n=2: \quad \frac{{@aa@}(2)}{(2)^2-{@bb@}}=\frac{{@aa*2@}}{{@(2)^2-bb@}}={@ta3@} \)</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \quad \quad n=3: \quad \frac{{@aa@}(3)}{(3)^2-{@bb@}}=\frac{{@aa*3@}}{{@(3)^2-bb@}}={@ta4@} \)</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \quad \quad n=4: \quad \frac{{@aa@}(4)}{(4)^2-{@bb@}}=\frac{{@aa*4@}}{{@(4)^2-bb@}}={@ta5@}\)</p>
<p>So, the first five terms of the sequence are, </p>
<p>\(\qquad \qquad \displaystyle \left\{ {@ta1@},{@ta2@},{@ta3@},{@ta4@},{@ta5@}, \dots \right\} \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
